    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d583">

                <pb facs="0559" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg483"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/17398</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Adjutant General to General Funston </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 10, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>President has directed that an armed force be sent into Mexico with the, sole
                    object of capturing Villa and preventing any further raids by his band, and with
                    scrupulous regard to sovereignty of Mexico. Secretary War directs you telegraph
                    exactly what you need in order to carry out foregoing general instructions, but
                    you will not take any overt steps until receipt definite orders from War
                    Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McCain</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
